to run samudra, gotta create software env and then execute some call

create software env; I use micromamba for quick iteration (but we will get this working with hpc-native stuff soon)

for pm-gpu this worked,

micromamba create -p /SOME/PATH/env  numpy=1 matplotlib-base xarray zarr=2 ipykernel cartopy xarrayutils dacite dask pandas cmocean scikit-learn ipywidgets requests aiohttp cftime einops nc-time-axis python=3.11 pytorch-gpu

micromamba activate /SOME/PATH/env

in root of repo, this runs:

torchrun src/train.py --config configs/train_samudra_om4.yaml


(pretty fast... note I had to reduce dims in configs because of mem issues)

